Z||000004||Gokart||08-29-2000||06:42 AM||||Start by taking the horn cover off and make sure you have the little spring thingy and the black piece of plastic dingy that slides in the spring. Sorry I couldn't resist <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||4
Z||000005||Carrolles||08-29-2000||08:48 AM||||First the obvious.  Check the BATT fuse (20 amp).  It also powers the cigar lighter, radio, courtesy lights (under the dash) and convenience center (the blue dingy thingy).<P>Then, like Gokart said, see if the wire inside the steering wheel under the horn button is connected.  It is usually a ground wire clipped onto the inside of the column.  When you push the horn button it completes a path to ground.  <P>The convenience center is located under the dash by the heater core.  This has the infamous Blue Dingy Thingy attached.  The horn relay is the square relay also mounted the the same box.  The flasher relay is the round one.<P>The following is from the 85 Helms manual:<P>1. Check the "Bat" Fuse by operating the LIGHT SWITCH.<P>2. If neither HORN will sound, ground the BLK wire of terminal B of the HORN RELAY. If the HORNS now sound, check for an open in the wiring to the HORN SWITCH.  If the HORNS do not sound, check the ORN wire at the HORN RELAY for battery voltage.  If battery voltage is present, replace the HORN RELAY.<P>3. THe HORNS may be tested by connecting a jumper from the connector on one of the HORNS (DK GRN wire) to the positive battery terminal.  The HORNS should sound.  If they do not sound, check the grounds and connectors.  Install new HORNS if no fault is found.<P>4. If the HORNS sound at all times, separate C210.  If the HORNS stop, check the HORN SWITCH and its wiring for a short to ground.  If the HORNS continue to sound with C210 separated, replace the HORN RELAY.<P>CIRCUIT OPERATION<P>When the HORN SWITCH is depressed, one side of the coil of the HORN RELAY is grounded.  The relay is enrgized. Its contacts close and apply battery voltage to the LO PITCH and HIGH PITCH HORNS.<P>COMPONENT LOCATION<P>Fuse block   Behind LH side of I/P<BR>Horn switch  Inside steering wheel<BR>Slip Ring    Top of steering column, below              steering wheel<BR>C100(34 cavities)  LH side of front bulkhead,                    right of brake master cylinder<BR>S210  Main harness, behind RH side of cluster.<P>Check out Oliver Scholz's "Illustrated Steering Column Disassembly" article at <P>wysiwyg://main.45/http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/steering.html<P>Hope this helps,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
